{"help": "https://open.canada.ca/data/api/3/action/help_show?name=package_show", "success": true, "result": {"aggregate_identifier": "", "association_type": [], "audience": [], "author": null, "author_email": null, "collection": "fgp", "contact_information": "{\"en\": {\"delivery_point\": \"560 Rochester Street\", \"city\": \"Ottawa\", \"administrative_area\": \"Ontario\", \"postal_code\": \"K1S 5K2\", \"country\": \"Canada\", \"electronic_mail_address\": \"FGP-PGF@NRCan-RNCan.gc.ca\"}, \"fr\": {\"point_de_livraison\": \"560 rue Rochester\", \"zone_administrative\": \"Ontario\", \"pays\": \"Canada (le)\", \"electronic_mail_address\": \"FGP-PGF@NRCan-RNCan.gc.ca\"}}", "contributor": {}, "creator": "", "creator_user_id": "b88b9549-3a4b-43a9-9375-5f3fc20fe782", "data_series_issue_identification": {}, "data_series_name": {}, "date_published": "2019-04-01 00:00:00", "display_flags": ["fgp_viewer"], "distributor": "{\"en\": {\"organization_name\": \"Government of Canada; Natural Resources Canada;Strategic Policy and Innovation Sector Canada, Centre for Mapping and Earth Observation, Federal Geospatial Platform\", \"address\": \"\", \"city\": \"Ottawa\", \"administrative_area\": \"Ontario\", \"postal_code\": \"\", \"country\": \"Canada\", \"electronic_mail_address\": \"FGP-PGF@NRCan-RNCan.gc.ca\"}, \"fr\": {\"nom_organization\": \"Gouvernement du Canada; Ressources naturelles Canada;Secteur de la politique strat\\u00e9gique et de l\\u2019innovation, Centre canadien de cartographie et d\\u2019observation de la Terre, Plateforme g\\u00e9ospatiale f\\u00e9d\\u00e9rale\", \"adresse\": \"\", \"zone_administrative\": \"Ontario\", \"pays\": \"Canada (le)\", \"electronic_mail_address\": \"FGP-PGF@NRCan-RNCan.gc.ca\"}}", "file_id": "a3dfbaf4-1b20-4061-aa0a-e7a79953f52d", "frequency": "not_planned", "geographic_region": [], "hierarchy_level": "dataset; jeuDonn\u00e9es", "id": "a3dfbaf4-1b20-4061-aa0a-e7a79953f52d", "imso_approval": "true", "isopen": false, "jurisdiction": "federal", "keywords": {"fr": ["R\u00e9gions physiographique du Canada", "Physiographie du Canada", "Environnement", "G\u00e9ologie", "Carte g\u00e9ologique"], "en": ["Physiographic Regions of Canada", "Physiography of Canada", "Environment", "Geology", "Geological maps"]}, "license_id": "ca-ogl-lgo", "license_title": "Open Government Licence - Canada", "license_url": "https://open.canada.ca/en/open-government-licence-canada", "maintainer": null, "maintainer_contact_form": {}, "maintainer_email": "FGP-PGF@NRCan-RNCan.gc.ca", "metadata_contact": {"fr": "Gouvernement du Canada; Ressources naturelles Canada;Secteur de la politique strat\u00e9gique et de l\u2019innovation, Centre canadien de cartographie et d\u2019observation de la Terre, Plateforme g\u00e9ospatiale f\u00e9d\u00e9rale, G\u00e9oConnaissances,FGP-PGF@NRCan-RNCan.gc.ca", "en": "Government of Canada; Natural Resources Canada;Strategic Policy and Innovation Sector Canada, Centre for Mapping and Earth Observation, Federal Geospatial Platform, GeoInsights,FGP-PGF@NRCan-RNCan.gc.ca"}, "metadata_created": "2020-02-25T15:15:05.322365", "metadata_modified": "2022-01-12T15:10:50.263989", "name": "a3dfbaf4-1b20-4061-aa0a-e7a79953f52d", "notes": "Canada\u2019s landmass is very diversified and comprises 7 distinctive areas called physiographic regions, each of which has its own unique topography and geology. Physiographic regions are large areas that share similar relief and landforms shaped by common geomorphic processes and geological history. Physiographic regions are often used to describe Canada\u2019s geography to show regional differences in climate, vegetation, population and the economy.  \n  \n  This dataset collection contains three interrelated datasets mapping the location of Canada\u2019s 7 different physiographic regions, their 21 subregions and many divisions (landforms).", "notes_translated": {"fr": "La masse continentale du Canada est tr\u00e8s diversifi\u00e9e et comprend sept r\u00e9gions distinctes appel\u00e9es r\u00e9gions physiographiques, chacune ayant sa propre topographie et g\u00e9ologie. Les r\u00e9gions physiographiques sont de vastes r\u00e9gions qui partagent des reliefs et topographies semblables form\u00e9s par des processus g\u00e9omorphologiques et une histoire g\u00e9ologique commune. Les r\u00e9gions physiographiques sont souvent utilis\u00e9es pour d\u00e9crire la g\u00e9ographie du Canada afin de montrer les diff\u00e9rentes r\u00e9gions de climat, v\u00e9g\u00e9tation, population et \u00e9conomie.  \n  \n  Ce rassemblement de donn\u00e9es contient trois ensembles de donn\u00e9es reli\u00e9s qui illustre l'emplacement des sept diff\u00e9rentes r\u00e9gions physiographiques du Canada, de leurs 21 sous-r\u00e9gions et de nombreuses divisions (formes de relief).", "en": "Canada\u2019s landmass is very diversified and comprises 7 distinctive areas called physiographic regions, each of which has its own unique topography and geology. Physiographic regions are large areas that share similar relief and landforms shaped by common geomorphic processes and geological history. Physiographic regions are often used to describe Canada\u2019s geography to show regional differences in climate, vegetation, population and the economy.  \n  \n  This dataset collection contains three interrelated datasets mapping the location of Canada\u2019s 7 different physiographic regions, their 21 subregions and many divisions (landforms)."}, "num_resources": 9, "num_tags": 0, "org_section": {}, "org_title_at_publication": {"fr": "Ressources naturelles Canada", "en": "Natural Resources Canada"}, "organization": {"id": "9391E0A2-9717-4755-B548-4499C21F917B", "name": "nrcan-rncan", "title": "Natural Resources Canada | Ressources naturelles Canada", "type": "organization", "description": "", "image_url": "", "created": "2016-09-23T17:25:46.737130", "is_organization": true, "approval_status": "approved", "state": "active"}, "owner_org": "9391E0A2-9717-4755-B548-4499C21F917B", "place_o